{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FE49etYmysqE249ArNtq5F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility implementations, `pkg/testutils/` provides differential testing, `pkg/sys/` wraps platform syscalls, `pkg/format/` provides shared formatting. Specs live in `docs/`.\n\n**Implementation status** (from source code, which takes precedence over stale metadata):\n- **Done**: pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/cat, cmd/wc, cmd/sponge, cmd/du (partial), cmd/ls (core), cmd/true, cmd/false, cmd/version\n- **Partial**: cmd/du has core traversal (R1.x, R4.x, R5.x) but empty `options` struct scaffolded for flags (-a, -s, -h, -c, -k, -d)\n- **Missing code, specs ready**: rel04.1 ls-extended\n- **Missing code, specs pending**: yes, basename, dirname, tee, head, seq\n\n**Earliest incomplete release with actionable work**: rel01.3 (du) — spec_complete but implementation is partial. The existing `cmd/du/main.go` implements core traversal (R1.x) with an explicitly empty options struct and a D3 comment noting scaffolding for display mode flags.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/du prd009-du R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R2.4 -- implement -a, -s, -c, -d display mode flags\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd009-du.yaml (full PRD -- locate requirements for display mode flags -a, -s, -c, -d; the R-numbers below are inferred from the existing code structure where R1.x is core traversal and R4.x/R5.x are error/signal handling; verify against the actual PRD and adjust implementation accordingly)\n      - cmd/du/main.go (existing implementation with empty options struct scaffolded for future flags per D3 comment)\n      - cmd/du/du_test.go (existing differential tests -- verify backward compatibility after changes)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/du/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add -a, -s, -c, -d flags to options struct and modify walkDir/duArg/main to implement them\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Add -a flag to options struct and register with flag.BoolVar: when active, print SIZE\\\\tPATH lines for individual non-directory files during recursive traversal, in addition to directory subtotals (prd009-du R2.1)\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Add -s flag to options struct and register with flag.BoolVar: when active, display only a single total line per command-line argument, suppressing all per-directory and per-file subtotals (prd009-du R2.2)\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Add -c flag to options struct and register with flag.BoolVar: when active, print a grand total line after processing all command-line arguments, using the same SIZE\\\\tPATH format with the path string total (prd009-du R2.3)\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Add -d N flag to options struct and register with flag.IntVar: when active, print totals only for directories at depth N or less below the command-line argument; depth 0 means print only the argument-level total (prd009-du R2.4)\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Read prd009-du.yaml before implementing. The R-numbers referenced in requirements (R2.1-R2.4) are inferred from the existing code structure. Verify the actual requirement IDs and acceptance criteria against the PRD and adjust the implementation to match the PRD specification.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the existing options struct and flag.BoolVar/flag.IntVar registration pattern in main(). The current options struct is empty with a D3 comment noting scaffolding for -a, -s, -h, -c, -k, -d flags. Add fields to this struct.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Modify walkDir to accept a depth parameter for -d tracking. Pass depth 0 from duArg and increment by 1 on recursive calls. When -a is active, print non-directory file entries in the traversal loop using the existing displayBlocks and fmt.Printf pattern. When -s is active, suppress the per-directory fmt.Printf at the end of walkDir.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"For -c grand total, modify duArg to return the total raw block count (int64, error) instead of just error. Accumulate returned block counts across arguments in main() and print a final total line using displayBlocks after the argument loop completes.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"The options struct has bool fields for -a, -s, -c and an int field for -d (max depth)\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"flag.Parse registers all four new flags with descriptive help text\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go build ./cmd/du/ compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Existing tests (go test ./cmd/du/) pass unchanged -- default behavior with no new flags is preserved\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"When -a is active, output includes SIZE\\\\tPATH lines for non-directory files within traversed directories\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"When -s is active, only one total line per argument is printed with no per-subdirectory lines\"\n      - id: AC7\n        text: \"When -c is active, a grand total line in SIZE\\\\ttotal format is printed after all arguments\"\n      - id: AC8\n        text: \"When -d N is active, directories deeper than N levels below the argument are traversed for block counting but their subtotal lines are not printed\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":93913,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":93913},"output_tokens":10,"se